# pr-413: gh-382 Parity with dm.ai#687: --key value override parsing must treat a value as JSON only when ALL of it is valid JSON

## Description

Closes #382
### What changed
Override values are parsed as JSON only when the whole trimmed string is a JSON array/object. `ADO` WIQL fragments are expanded to a full `SELECT` before the `wit/wiql` POST.

### Key decisions
- `_parseOverrideValue` (run_command_processor.dart): decode the trimmed value; on `FormatException` or non-container result, keep the original string (parity with Java dm.ai#688).
- `expandWiql` (ado_client.dart): top-level helper, `SELECT\b` regex (case-insensitive, leading whitespace), so `selection = 1` stays a WHERE fragment; null/blank pass through.
- Tests mirror the cases listed in gh-382.

### How to verify
```bash
dart test test/cli/run_command_processor_test.dart test/integrations/ado/
```
Result: 167 passed; `dart analyze lib/src/cli lib/src/integrations/ado` clean; `dart format` clean.
Full suite not run in this session.
# PR Diff Truncated

Original size: 14170 characters.
Kept: first 7800 and last 4200 characters.

The full diff is available in the checked-out PR branch. Use `git diff` or CodeGraph for focused source navigation instead of relying only on this file.

```diff
diff --git a/lib/src/cli/run_command_processor.dart b/lib/src/cli/run_command_processor.dart
index 4275a232..10228f67 100644
--- a/lib/src/cli/run_command_processor.dart
+++ b/lib/src/cli/run_command_processor.dart
@@ -112,9 +112,19 @@ class RunCommandProcessor {
   /// - Strings starting with `[` → JSON arrays.
   /// - Strings starting with `{` → JSON objects.
   /// - Other strings → left as strings.
+  ///
+  /// Structured JSON is applied only when the WHOLE trimmed string decodes to
+  /// an array or object (parity with Java dm.ai#688). Any decode failure or
+  /// trailing text keeps the original string.
   dynamic _parseOverrideValue(String value) {
-    if (value.startsWith('[') || value.startsWith('{')) {
-      return jsonDecode(value);
+    final trimmed = value.trim();
+    if (trimmed.startsWith('[') || trimmed.startsWith('{')) {
+      try {
+        final decoded = jsonDecode(trimmed);
+        if (decoded is List || decoded is Map) return decoded;
+      } on FormatException {
+        // Not valid JSON as a whole — keep the raw string.
+      }
     }
     return value;
   }
diff --git a/lib/src/integrations/ado/ado_client.dart b/lib/src/integrations/ado/ado_client.dart
index bb17de66..7ef62a69 100644
--- a/lib/src/integrations/ado/ado_client.dart
+++ b/lib/src/integrations/ado/ado_client.dart
@@ -16,6 +16,20 @@ import 'ado_json.dart';
 import 'ado_work_item_client.dart';
 import 'ado_work_item_ops.dart';

+/// Matches a query that begins with the `SELECT` keyword (any case, leading
+/// whitespace allowed). The trailing `\b` keeps fields such as `selection`
+/// from matching.
+final RegExp _selectStatement = RegExp(r'^\s*select\b', caseSensitive: false);
+
+/// Expands a short WIQL fragment (e.g. `System.State = 'Active'`) into a full
+/// statement, matching Java `AzureDevOpsClient.expandWiql`. Full `SELECT`
+/// statements, and null/blank input, pass through unchanged.
+String? expandWiql(String? wiql) {
+  if (wiql == null || wiql.trim().isEmpty) return wiql;
+  if (_selectStatement.hasMatch(wiql)) return wiql;
+  return 'SELECT [System.Id] FROM WorkItems WHERE $wiql';
+}
+
 /// Azure DevOps API methods exposed to the MCP tool runtime.
 class AdoClient {
   final AdoHttpClient _http;
@@ -148,7 +162,7 @@ class AdoClient {
       {List<String>? fields}) async {
     final body = await _http.post(
       'wit/wiql',
-      body: jsonEncode({'query': wiql}),
+      body: jsonEncode({'query': expandWiql(wiql)}),
     );
     final decoded = jsonDecode(body);
     final ids = decoded is Map && decoded['workItems'] is List
